# ===== Process mirror (client worktrees) =====
# deliver/process/ is tracked on main only. scripts/scenario.mjs mirrors the started scenarios and
# their toolkits into a client folder from the `main` ref, and the mirror is never tracked, so a fix
# to the process can only land on main. A client tracks its README, RUNBOOK, docs/ and each step's
# output/. FIRST in this file on purpose: the media and profile rules below still win inside output/.
/deliver/brandklout/*/scenario-*/**
!/deliver/brandklout/*/scenario-*/**/
!/deliver/brandklout/*/scenario-*/*/output/**
/deliver/brandklout/*/tools/
/deliver/brandklout/*/.process-mirror.json

# ===== Workflow Artifacts =====
# .tmp folders are committed when they contain lightweight workflow artifacts.
# Heavy binary/media files inside .tmp remain excluded by the asset rules below.
# Browser style-capture fetched resource mirrors are noisy third-party caches;
# keep resource-urls.json instead.
# Rendered-DOM mirrors from content-intake captures are the same kind of noisy
# third-party cache (~7.5MB for one client). The structured meta.json extracted
# from each one is committed instead, and capture.mjs re-fetches the raw page.
**/01-content-intake/.tmp/**/rendered.html
**/01-content-intake/.tmp/**/*.rendered.html
# Throwaway Chrome profiles created by the headless QA harnesses. Tens of MB of
# browser state per run, regenerated on every invocation.
# Throwaway Chrome profiles for the driven QA harnesses. Each harness makes its
# own so two runs cannot collide; the glob saves enumerating every new one.
**/.chrome-*/

# Headless-Chrome user-data dirs from verification harnesses. These land inside
# .tmp/ and contain paths longer than Git can index on Windows.
**/.chrome-profile/
**/.chrome-dbg/

# ===== Secrets =====
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Google OAuth client downloads — they belong in ~/.brandklout/, never in a repo.
client_secret_*.json
# Instatic login cookies written by the API toolkits (.session-<host>).
.session-*

# ===== Binary / Media Assets =====
# Heavy binary/media assets are backed up to Cloudflare R2 by scripts/assets.mjs (manifest: <client>/assets.tsv).
# Never commit these file types to Git.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.avif
*.svg
*.ico
*.pdf
*.mp4
*.webm
*.mov
*.zip
*.7z
*.psd
*.ai
*.eps
*.fig
*.sketch
# Web fonts. Scraped-site mirrors pull in whole Elementor/FontAwesome families
# and Google Fonts subsets — ~290 files from a single WordPress theme, 8.9MB from
# one capture. None are licensed brand typefaces and none are client deliverables;
# the asset catalogue records them instead. Same rule as the images above: the VPS
# is the source of truth.
*.ttf
*.otf
*.woff
*.woff2
*.eot

# Raw server-rendered HTML saved by scrape_site.py --save-html. 19 MB for one
# 91-page site, and re-fetchable. The per-page .md extracts and .json records
# next to it are the committed artifact.
**/.tmp/**/html/

# ===== Python =====
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/

# ===== Dependencies / Local Test Output =====
node_modules/
test-results/
**/pw-profile/

# ===== OS / IDE =====
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Obsidian's open-tab / pane state. Per-machine UI churn, and it kept a stale
# pointer to a Webzite agency file alive inside this Brandklout-only repo.
# The rest of .obsidian/ (app.json, graph.json, core-plugins.json, appearance.json)
# IS tracked on purpose: it is the shared vault setup, so the graph looks the same
# on every machine. Everything below is per-machine state or a local cache.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json
.trash/
*.swp
*.swo

# Session rotation working state (SYSTEM_RULES.md section 5).
# Deliberately untracked: every worktree writes the same path, so tracking it would
# guarantee a merge conflict on every client branch. The durable record of what a
# session did is its commits; the runbook is only the handoff between sessions.
# Runbooks are TRACKED as of 2026-09-04. A client's history lives at
# deliver/brandklout/<client>/docs/RUNBOOK.md + docs/runbook/, and the repo's own
# system history at .claude/RUNBOOK.md + .claude/runbook/. Ignoring them meant they
# travelled with nothing, were backed up nowhere, and died with the worktree.
# Nothing below re-ignores them.

# Leftovers from the session-rotation hooks removed on 2026-08-22 (SYSTEM_RULES.md
# section 5). Kept ignored so old worktrees do not surface them as new files.
.claude/session-state.json
.claude/rotate.lock

# ===== Logs =====
*.log
logs/

# ===== Throwaway browser profiles =====
# Headless verification spawns Chrome with --user-data-dir. A profile left behind
# in a workflow's .tmp/ is thousands of tiny files, several of them with paths too
# long for Windows git to stat — which turns every `git status` and every commit
# into a multi-minute walk over files nobody wants tracked.
.chrome-bisect/
.chrome-profile/
chrome-profile-*/

# Orca per-worktree briefs and review notes — deliberately local, never committed (959b916)
.orca-*.md

# Dr. Nahlah source material — kept on disk in the bk-dr-nahlah worktree for
# context, never committed: scraped WordPress assets and client-supplied media.
# 03-graphic-resources/.tmp/downloads also breaks `git add` outright on Windows
# ("Filename too long") on the Elementor google-fonts woff2 names.
deliver/brandklout/dr-nahlah/workflows/03-graphic-resources/.tmp/downloads/
deliver/brandklout/dr-nahlah/workflows/01-content-intake/.tmp/current-site-scrape/
deliver/brandklout/dr-nahlah/workflows/00-client-delivery-initialization/.tmp/client-handoff/
deliver/brandklout/dr-nahlah/workflows/00-client-delivery-initialization/.tmp/design-system/

# Windows reserved device names, created by stray `> nul` redirects. Git cannot
# open them ("No such file or directory") and `git add -A` dies on the whole run.
nul
[Cc][Oo][Nn]
[Pp][Rr][Nn]
[Aa][Uu][Xx]

# Cached admin session cookies. `insta-api.mjs` writes one next to itself on
# first login; it is a live credential for a client's CMS. The Dr. Nahlah copy
# was protected by a local .tmp/.gitignore, which only helps the folder that
# happens to have one - this covers every copy of the toolkit, including the
# shared module in deliver/process/.
**/.tmp/.session

# --- 2026-09-09: worktree hygiene ---------------------------------------------
# Repo-ROOT .tmp/ is ad-hoc session scratch, not a workflow artifact folder. In
# bk-stone-dental it held 3.6MB of MCP tool-schema dumps, image previews and a
# live session token. Workflow artifacts belong in that workflow's own .tmp/.
/.tmp/

# MCP/admin session tokens. Same class as **/.tmp/.session above: a live
# credential written next to the script that minted it.
**/.tmp/mcp-session.txt
**/.tmp/mcp-call.py

# Editors keep creating these empty files at the repo root.
/untitled*.md

# ── Step output folders (scenario layout, 2026-09-23) ─────────────────────────
# Every scenario step has an output/ folder (it replaced .tmp/). Lightweight text
# artifacts, code and the step RUNBOOK.md are committed; media stays out through the
# extension rules above and is backed up to R2. The .tmp rules above stay for client
# branches that still use the old layout.
**/output/**/html/
**/output/.session
**/output/mcp-session.txt
**/output/mcp-call.py
**/output/**/node_modules/

# Asana pulls are per-person task dumps, regenerated on demand
deliver/scripts/output/
# A tool run from its own folder writes output/ beside the scripts; run output is never system code.
deliver/process/tools/*/output/

# Run outputs recovered from the per-worktree deliver/process copies on 2026-09-27 (backups, bundles,
# logs). Too large or too raw for git; scripts/assets.mjs keeps them in R2.
deliver/brandklout/*/process-outputs/

# ===== Rules the client branches carried in their own .gitignore (merged 2026-09-27) =====
# SSH keys and anything a host hands us.
.secrets/
*.pem
id_ed25519*
id_rsa*
!*.pub
# Per-host Instatic login caches (.session-<host>). The trailing * is load bearing: a bare
# `.session` pattern stopped matching when the cache went per-host and nearly committed a cookie.
**/.tmp/.session*
# A scrape's live PHPSESSID, and its third-party asset mirror (1.2 GB, paths past Windows' limit).
**/.tmp/site-scrape/.state/cookies.json
**/.tmp/site-scrape/assets/
# Recovered client data: DB dumps carry credentials and patient-adjacent PII. Local only, not in R2.
**/recovered/
# Rendered-DOM mirrors off a compromised WordPress install; meta.json and rendered.txt stay tracked.
**/01-site-recovery/.tmp/pages/**/rendered.html
# Raw PHP error logs copied off client servers.
php_errorlog
# Instatic import bundles, regenerated by to-instatic.mjs.
**/.tmp/instatic/
# Dr. Nahlah's Instatic run output: page backups and parity snapshots, all regenerable.
deliver/brandklout/dr-nahlah/workflows/15-instatic-api-sync/.tmp/
deliver/brandklout/dr-nahlah/workflows/22-instatic-api-sync/.tmp/
# Mason Park landing pages: CDN images, screenshots and regenerated JSON.
deliver/brandklout/mason-park/workflows/10-lp-instatic/.tmp/capture/assets/
deliver/brandklout/mason-park/workflows/10-lp-instatic/.tmp/compare/
deliver/brandklout/mason-park/workflows/10-lp-instatic/.tmp/converted-pages.json
deliver/brandklout/mason-park/workflows/10-lp-instatic/.tmp/preview.log
# Stone's Google Drive export, including identifiable before/after patient photos (see its HANDOFF.md).
deliver/brandklout/stone-surgical-arts/workflows/01-content-intake/.tmp/google-drive-images/
# Packed client-review builds, regenerated by make-preview.mjs.
deliver/brandklout/*/workflows/04-design/.tmp/*/preview-*.html

# webflow-clientfirst MCP writes generated vocabularies and resolved payloads here; regenerate them.
mcp-servers/webflow-clientfirst/.tmp/
